# OctoAcme Project Management Docs

A guide to OctoAcme’s project management processes and practices. Use this README as the starting point for understanding the lifecycle and finding detailed guidance.

## Project management process summary

OctoAcme manages cross-functional work through five stages: initiate and validate the need; plan scope, milestones, resources, risks, and backlog; execute in small increments while tracking progress and quality; release with verification and rollback plans; and close with a retrospective and actionable improvements. Project Managers coordinate delivery, risks, and communication, while Product Managers define outcomes and priorities. Teams use project boards, regular delivery and stakeholder updates, clear acceptance criteria, testing, and documented decisions to maintain alignment.

