## Lifecycle at a glance

1. Initiation: confirm the business need, stakeholders, success metrics, and whether to move forward.
2. Planning: turn the approved idea into a prioritized backlog, milestone map, resources plan, and risk register.
3. Execution: track progress on a project board, hold standups and reviews, and manage blockers and dependencies.
4. Release: verify readiness, deploy through controlled checks, and communicate changes and rollback plans.
5. Close & improvement: capture lessons learned and convert them into actionable improvements for the next cycle.

## How to use these docs

Start with the project overview and then open the document that matches the work phase or topic. Keep the project charter and other artifacts updated in the repo so the team has a single source of truth for decisions, risks, and delivery status.
